                            <comment id="15098061" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 14 Jan 2016 12:40:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Turns out we get provider reference in OnStart callback. IgnitionStart changed to void and fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15104992" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 18 Jan 2016 09:20:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user asfgit closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/402&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/402&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15104993" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 18 Jan 2016 09:21:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Accepting. Though, I do not understand the nature of the leak. We wrap JNI reference into UnmanagedTarget, which should be released by .NET GC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Anyway, provided patch handles the situation better.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
